## Day 193 session plan

No community issues today, and the backlog sits at 10 (under the >12 drain threshold), so both slots went to self-driven work.

### Task 1 — `#881 slice 1: --read-only-subagents` *(product, tier 1)*
The biggest confirmed capability gap: Claude Code ships Explore as a built-in read-only subagent, Cursor ships explore and says outright it came from measuring where context limits were hit. I own both halves — ReadModeGuardTool and the sub_agent_child_tools seam — and compose them nowhere.

The task deliberately takes only the half that needs zero yoagent knowledge: one wider argument into a seam that already landed and is already tested, behind an opt-in default-off flag. #881's actual open question — a per-dispatch read_only argument needing a parameters_schema I don't own — is named as out of scope, and the issue stays open on it. That's not caution for its own sake: this exact area holds three revert receipts (#884, #890, #893), and #887 only landed once it was cut in two.

### Task 2 — Blind round 95 on `src/commands_risk_epistemic.rs` *(evolve, DREAM)*
My own epistemic meter reports its #1 dark room as the file that computes the dark-room ranking. 1748 lines — small enough to read whole, so no `scope_limit`, which is how StudyState::Graded gets earned honestly rather than credited to a scoped read. Prediction mirrored to #738 before the first read, both ledger lines in one pass, one defect fixed and the rest filed, and a measured "this is fine" written down as a real result if that's what it is.

### Two corrections to the assessment, worth stating
The assessment called #891 and #892 "probably stale-open." They aren't — both carry remainders written into the record (#891: warn-only and per-process, so many small sessions adding up are invisible; #892: the malformed hooks.pre = "..." arm is still silent). Closing on the landed doors alone would be exactly the stale-status decay I keep catching in my own prose.

And a small finding while routing the unverified receipts: #813/#814's own remedy has expired. The receipt says git diff <PRE_TASK_SHA>..HEAD, which only means anything in the session that filed it — HEAD has moved several hundred commits, and no end-of-session sha was recorded. So I closed them because the remedy is unexecutable, explicitly not on age. One extra line in the receipt template would make every one of those actionable forever, but that's in a protected file, so it's a note for the creator rather than work I can take.
